      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm maybe we can sync on this. Android\u0027s CHRE does something very similar which I thought could apply here too. For example, they have sensor samples which look like:\n\n```\nstruct sample_data {\n  struct sample_data_header header; //\u003c Header includes num_samples which must\n                                    //  always be at least 1\n  struct data {\n    ...\n  } samples[1];\n};\n```\n\nWhat this does is that the common case can be allocated with a simple `struct sample_data data`, but if you want multiple samples you can just allocate\n\n```\nuint8_t buffer[sizeof(struct sample_data) + (n-1) * sizeof(struct data)];\nstruct sample_data *data \u003d buffer; //\u003c has n samples allocated\ndata-\u003eheader-\u003enum_samples \u003d n;\n```",
